A||||4||DougV||4 speed to 5 speed??||||1||
Z||000000||DougV||11-28-2000||09:42 PM||||I'd like to convert my 86 SE 4-speed to 5-speed. I have a 87 5-speed 4cyl. parts car. what is involved in this coversion/ Thanx<BR>Doug Venner<BR>85 GT<BR>86 SE<BR>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||11-29-2000||09:48 AM||||You just need to swap over trans, slave cylinder for clutch, shifter cables and the lower portion of the shifter (you can just swap the entire shifter) We swapped a 4-spd to a Getreg 5-spd, I think the Izusu (4-cyl 5-spd) Is also a direct swap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wilburt||11-29-2000||06:14 PM||||I'm not sure if this apply's to the '86, but some 4 speeds have the back-up light switch on the shifter asm., and the 5 speeds have the switch on the trans. Just splice from the shifter to the trans. Hope this helps. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Elenor84||11-30-2000||05:07 PM||||Could this also be done on a 84 2m4?<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
Z||000004||wilburt||11-30-2000||09:35 PM||||Yes. I just removed a 4.10 out of an '84 (for another project), and replaced it with an '85 5-speed. No problems at all except for the back-up light switch.||||reg||14
